// `clock()` and `args()` in the AOT backend (BACKLOG §6 item 25).
//
// Both read a value the chunk can only obtain at entry, so both travel through
// a hidden global: `$clockOrigin` holds the monotonic counter captured before
// the first statement (so `clock()` is elapsed time, not an absolute counter)
// and `$args` holds the array the entry point builds from `(argc, argv)`.
//
// `clock()` is only asserted by its *shape*, never a value: two runs happen at
// different times and the harness runs the VM and the binary separately.
// `args()` is asserted by content, because the harness passes the same vector to
// both (`-DOSKEL_ARGS`), including one argument with a space in it -- a naive
// tokeniser would split that one in two.

var a = clock();
print("clock type", type(a));
print("clock non-negative", a >= 0.0);
var b = clock();
print("clock monotonic", b >= a);

var rest = args();
print("args type", type(rest));
print("args count", len(rest));
var i = 0;
for (a in rest) {
  print("arg", i, a);
  i = i + 1;
}
